# Large derived artifacts — never commit; ship a `make data` download
# script instead (§8.0: "Never commit large binaries to the repo directly").
*.npy
*.jsonl
*.db

# Data and model downloads (catalog.jsonl, the embedding matrix, the
# MiniLM checkpoint) — regenerated by the offline stage (§3.2).
data/
models/

# ...except the fitted ranker, which is committed. §8.0's rule is about
# large binaries (catalog.jsonl is 60MB, embeddings.npy 77MB); this is a
# 1.5KB JSON of eleven coefficients. Committing it is what makes the
# headline score reproducible: the evaluator is fully deterministic against
# a fixed ranker, whereas refitting draws a new corpus and lands anywhere in
# a 0.033-wide band. A clean clone without it silently falls back to
# hand-set weights and scores well below the headline.
!models/
!models/ranker.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Notebooks (§8.0: "Notebooks for exploration only")
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Organizer-supplied kit (not authored by this team, like data/ and models/)
kit/*
!kit/README.md
